# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# `.env` is gitignored — it must exist in LOCAL checkouts only, never in git.
#
# These are the Firebase Web SDK config values for the vedadarshi-admin web app
# (Firebase project vedadarshi-20989, app id 1:1029956122:web:16ac52d8bbb0f35e0327a3).
#
# Note on secrecy: the Firebase WEB config is a public client identifier — Vite
# inlines every VITE_* value into the built JS bundle, so it is readable by
# anyone who loads the admin panel. It is not protected by keeping it out of
# git. Access is controlled by Firestore security rules and (later) App Check.
# It is kept out of git as policy, not because these values are secret.
#
# The keys that genuinely MUST stay server-side are different ones — the OpenAI
# key and the Vedika API key. Those belong in Cloud Functions config and must
# never appear in this file or anywhere in the client.
#
# To repopulate the real values: Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps
# → vedadarshi-admin (web), or the Firebase MCP `firebase_get_sdk_config` tool
# with app_id 1:1029956122:web:16ac52d8bbb0f35e0327a3.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=
